WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:04.180
All right, so let's sort of close the loop
on our coverage of the Gates situation, I

00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:10.589
told you last segment that Donald Trump had
to be talked out of publicly defending Matt

00:00:10.589 --> 00:00:14.719
Gates because the believed allegations against
him are so serious.

00:00:14.719 --> 00:00:18.500
Now, in the next segment, you will see that
Matt Gates is still claiming that he has support

00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:19.500
from Donald Trump.

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:24.939
But breaking this morning, a report from CNN
that Matt Gates tried to meet with Donald

00:00:24.939 --> 00:00:26.940
Trump and was denied such a meeting.

00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:33.640
It seems as though Donald Trump has been thoroughly
convinced by his aides and staffers that Matt

00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:35.610
Gates is completely toxic right now.

00:00:35.610 --> 00:00:39.079
And actually, this fits very much within what
we know about Donald Trump.

00:00:39.079 --> 00:00:40.600
And I'll get into that in a moment.

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:45.829
The report from CNN is that Congressman Matt
Gates, facing a federal investigation into

00:00:45.829 --> 00:00:50.140
sex trafficking allegations, recently was
denied a meeting that he tried to get with

00:00:50.140 --> 00:00:53.280
Donald Trump at Trump's Mar a Lago estate.

00:00:53.280 --> 00:01:00.410
As Trump and allies continue to distance from
the Florida congressman, two people familiar

00:01:00.410 --> 00:01:07.860
with the matter say that Gates tried to schedule
a visit with Donald Trump after it was revealed

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:09.850
that he was being investigated.

00:01:09.850 --> 00:01:14.540
But the request was rejected by aides close
to Donald Trump, who, as I mentioned to you

00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:19.410
in the previous segment, are telling Trump,
don't stick your neck out for this guy.

00:01:19.410 --> 00:01:22.020
Don't defend Matt Gates.

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:28.659
Harlan Hill, who is a spokesman for Gates,
is denying it and saying no such meeting was

00:01:28.659 --> 00:01:29.659
requested.

00:01:29.659 --> 00:01:35.630
And that actually Gates was welcomed to Trump
Doral this weekend and didn't try to meet

00:01:35.630 --> 00:01:37.180
with Donald Trump.

00:01:37.180 --> 00:01:43.200
Now, my instinct is that this is, of course,
if you are if you're Matt Gates, you request

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:45.579
the meeting through staff.

00:01:45.579 --> 00:01:49.729
And if it's rejected, the staff simply deny
having requested it.

00:01:49.729 --> 00:01:54.230
And if you're Matt Gates, you can accurately
say, I never requested anything.

00:01:54.230 --> 00:01:58.290
So if you say, well, how do I adjudicate the
differences between the claims that are being

00:01:58.290 --> 00:01:59.290
made?

00:01:59.290 --> 00:02:05.039
It's it's quite obvious to me that this is
exactly what the way it would work if indeed,

00:02:05.039 --> 00:02:08.810
Matt Gates quietly tried to get the meeting
and it was rejected.

00:02:08.810 --> 00:02:14.630
CNN writes that the interference by Trump's
aides signals that Gates is increasingly isolated

00:02:14.630 --> 00:02:19.730
as he weathers a potentially career ending
scandal just months after he offered to leave

00:02:19.730 --> 00:02:23.710
his job to join Trump's impeachment defense
team.

00:02:23.710 --> 00:02:28.830
Comedically, Gates joining the impeachment
defense team may have been more substantive

00:02:28.830 --> 00:02:33.740
as far as you know, like Saturday Night Live
writers are concerned, but this may actually

00:02:33.740 --> 00:02:38.530
be a much more interesting sort of going down
in flames for Matt Gates.

00:02:38.530 --> 00:02:43.930
Now, you'll also remember that last week it
was revealed and reported that Matt Gates

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:48.280
tried to get a blanket preemptive pardon from
Donald Trump at the end of Donald Trump's

00:02:48.280 --> 00:02:51.990
presidency that has also been denied by Donald
Trump.

00:02:51.990 --> 00:02:54.840
Trump claiming Gates did not ask me for a
pardon.

00:02:54.840 --> 00:03:00.740
Again, with all of these things, it's possible
that Gates staffers went to Trump staffers

00:03:00.740 --> 00:03:03.130
and said, would this work?

00:03:03.130 --> 00:03:05.410
Trump staffers would have said he's not going
to do that.

00:03:05.410 --> 00:03:08.840
And as far as Trump knows, it was never an
official request.

00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:11.280
And so nobody is really lying.

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:15.220
But the spirit of this is that Gates did want
the pardon.

00:03:15.220 --> 00:03:20.710
That's often, you know, in political speak,
the way this is all orchestrated is to have

00:03:20.710 --> 00:03:22.380
that plausible deniability.

00:03:22.380 --> 00:03:27.210
Trump can say, I was never asked to pardon
him and that can be true.

00:03:27.210 --> 00:03:33.730
While it can also be true that Gates directed
staff to fill out Trump staff as to whether

00:03:33.730 --> 00:03:36.480
it's something that might be possible.

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:43.360
Now, the other kind of question about the
meeting being denied between Gates and Trump

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:51.070
is that Gates was at this event in Florida,
and although he didn't meet privately with

00:03:51.070 --> 00:03:55.480
Trump, you would think that that has some
meaning, that he was still sort of allowed

00:03:55.480 --> 00:03:59.220
to participate at the other on the other end.

00:03:59.220 --> 00:04:01.300
What can Trump really even do for Gates at
this point?

00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:06.070
I mean, it seems that at this point the story
is so out of the bag, either Republican's

00:04:06.070 --> 00:04:08.900
big picture are just going to start ignoring
it.

00:04:08.900 --> 00:04:12.960
And Matt Gates will be able to survive this
and won't have to resign or Gates is basically

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:14.080
going to be done for.

00:04:14.080 --> 00:04:18.160
But beyond just repeating the same lies that
Gates is telling, I don't really know what

00:04:18.160 --> 00:04:22.750
Trump can do for Gates at this point in time
when Trump was president.

00:04:22.750 --> 00:04:28.770
Lying about himself to some degree worked
in another sense it didn't, because Trump

00:04:28.770 --> 00:04:33.560
lost and he lost the House for Republicans
and he lost the Senate, but it at least kept

00:04:33.560 --> 00:04:38.190
Trump afloat amidst some scandals.

00:04:38.190 --> 00:04:42.100
Trump as a former president, telling lies
in defense of Matt Gates.

00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:44.490
It's not really clear to me that it would
do very much.

00:04:44.490 --> 00:04:48.130
Now, one last thought on this before we move
on to what Matt Gates is actually saying about

00:04:48.130 --> 00:04:50.560
all of these things.

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:54.770
Loyalty is a one way street with Donald Trump.

00:04:54.770 --> 00:05:01.320
Matt Gates was completely loyal to a sort
of disgusting, sycophantic level during Trump's

00:05:01.320 --> 00:05:02.350
presidency.

00:05:02.350 --> 00:05:05.850
But Gates is no longer useful to Donald Trump.

00:05:05.850 --> 00:05:10.450
Once you're no longer useful to Trump or you
have your own problems, Trump tosses you aside

00:05:10.450 --> 00:05:13.300
like he's done to so many people in his life.

00:05:13.300 --> 00:05:15.700
Eventually, it's always just a matter of time.

00:05:15.700 --> 00:05:17.900
So that's the latest from Trump.

00:05:17.900 --> 00:05:19.780
Let's now look at some of the very strange
things that Matt Gates said

